codex
The paper’s source confirms an important Step 0 fact already: its results are algorithms, not computational hardness results. In particular, it explicitly discusses a sequential greedy coloring route and later bounds its own internal computation. That rules out an honest Track A claim for theorem-regime instances, but it may support Track B if the measured mechanical route is large and the generated instances expose a genuinely short structural compression. I’m reading the proof sections now to determine whether that gap exists.
